{"id": 1911, "date": "2015-02-19T11:00:47", "date_gmt": "2015-02-19T19:00:47", "guid": {"rendered": "http://estreetshuffle.com/?p=1911"}, "modified": "2026-07-21T14:07:16", "modified_gmt": "2026-07-21T21:07:16", "slug": "cover-me-burning-love", "status": "publish", "type": "post", "link": "https://estreetshuffle.com/index.php/2015/02/19/cover-me-burning-love/", "title": {"rendered": "Burning Love"}, "content": {"rendered": "<p>It&#8217;s always a fun moment when &#8220;Burning Love&#8221; shows up in the setlist. Arthur Alexander&#8217;s 1972 brassy, swinging classic (made famous when Elvis Presley covered it shortly after) is perfectly suited for the super-sized E Street Band of recent years.</p>\n<p>Here&#8217;s Bruce covering it in Nashville in 2014:</p>\n<div class=\"jetpack-video-wrapper\"><span class=\"embed-youtube\" style=\"text-align:center; display: block;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" class=\"youtube-player\" width=\"758\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/00USiPVj23M?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border:0;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"></iframe></span></div>\n<p>&#8230;and again in 2026:</p>\n<div class=\"jetpack-video-wrapper\"><span class=\"embed-youtube\" style=\"text-align:center; display: block;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" class=\"youtube-player\" width=\"758\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/uf5BX50qElQ?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border:0;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"></iframe></span></div>\n<p>But Bruce doesn&#8217;t need the band to rock this tune&#8211;here he is taking requests on his acoustic guitar in a Paris pre-show in 2013:</p>\n<div class=\"jetpack-video-wrapper\"><span class=\"embed-youtube\" style=\"text-align:center; display: block;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" class=\"youtube-player\" width=\"758\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/FYqQNIPd96g?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border:0;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"></iframe></span></div>\n<p>The &#8220;hunka hunka&#8217;s&#8221; are dead giveaways that Bruce has Elvis&#8217; version in mind when he plays the song, but I&#8217;m more partial to the original below. If you haven&#8217;t heard it before, give it a listen&#8211;the arrangement would have been right at home on the Wrecking Ball and High Hopes Tours.</p>\n<div class=\"jetpack-video-wrapper\"><span class=\"embed-youtube\" style=\"text-align:center; display: block;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" class=\"youtube-player\" width=\"758\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/fKDF5AM3O4k?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border:0;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"></iframe></span></div>\n<p><strong>Burning Love<br />\nFirst performed:</strong> April 12, 1995 (New York City, NY)<br />\n<strong>Last performed:</strong> June 5, 2026 (West Long Branch, NJ)</p>\n<p>\u00a9 May 1, 2018</p>\n", "protected": false}, "excerpt": {"rendered": "<p>Acoustic or electric, Bruce has fun with this Arthur Alexander/Elvis Presley classic.</p>\n", "protected": false}, "author": 1, "featured_media": 70747, "comment_status": "open", "ping_status": "open", "sticky": false, "template": "", 